(3683643, 512810, 5792, '<td valign="top">One of the most technically perfect natural floral images I''ve seen in a long time. I gave it a 10 and would anytime. Simply gorgious. Great job!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-05-23 00:54:04.</i></td>', 'One of the most technically perfect natural floral images I''ve seen in a long time. I gave it a 10 and would anytime. Simply gorgious. Great job!', '2007-05-23 01:51:59.000000', '2007-05-23 01:54:04.000000', 0),
(3683663, 512490, 37104, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>First of all, great composition! You put the fish in the right place in the frame and used other elements to draw attention back to it! I think the texture in this picture is great, some people may have found it hard to associate this with "Silky-Smooth," but I think it works.<br/> <br/>One of your biggest problems is the depth of field. It is very shallow, making too much of the picture blurry. I think a more shallow depth of field is appropriate for this picture, but this is far too much. While the colors in the picture are evident, they aren''t flattering. There are a lot of dull browns and greens that, although they are in great contrast with the fish, aren''t appealing to the eye of the viewer. The lighting of this picture also looks very unnatural. <br/> <br/>The composition of the shot is terrific, but if you had spent more time on lighting, aperture, etc. it would be much nicer. Unfortunately, you said this was a last-minute shot. For the next one, try to spend more time getting the technicals down if you can. <br/> <br/>--James B. Hale</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!! First of all, great composition! You put the fish in the right place in the frame and used other elements to draw attention back to it! I think the texture in this picture is great, some people may have found it hard to associate this with "Silky-Smooth," but I think it works. One of your biggest problems is the depth of field. It is very shallow, making too much of the picture blurry. I think a more shallow depth of field is appropriate for this picture, but this is far too much. While the colors in the picture are evident, they aren''t flattering. There are a lot of dull browns and greens that, although they are in great contrast with the fish, aren''t appealing to the eye of the viewer. The lighting of this picture also looks very unnatural.  The composition of the shot is terrific, but if you had spent more time on lighting, aperture, etc. it would be much nicer. Unfortunately, you said this was a last-minute shot. For the next one, try to spend more time getting the technicals down if you can.  --James B. Hale', '2007-05-23 01:54:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3683668, 511473, 50641, '<td valign="top">Love it.  7 from me but I don''t think it counted.  The light at the top is great.</td>', 'Love it.  7 from me but I don''t think it counted.  The light at the top is great.', '2007-05-23 01:55:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3683677, 510090, 69260, '<td valign="top">The final result is now published ...and I''m very happy with it because I could not imagine I could reach Nb 23 with this image and so few participations in this challenge !<br/>I want to thank very much all of you who gave their vote to my image, on the other hand your comments were a great encouragement to me and confirmed I could perhaps go on posting some pics in the future !<br/>Thanks again !!<br/>Pol (pfgbel)</td>', 'The final result is now published ...and I''m very happy with it because I could not imagine I could reach Nb 23 with this image and so few participations in this challenge !I want to thank very much all of you who gave their vote to my image, on the other hand your comments were a great encouragement to me and confirmed I could perhaps go on posting some pics in the future !Thanks again !!Pol (pfgbel)', '2007-05-23 01:57:01.000000', NULL, 0),
