(3689452, 512486, 60173, '<td valign="top">People say that brighter colors would have made them like this photo more. To me brighter colors would have made this cliche. It''s the colors that really make this photo. It''s very soothing. Very Silky Smooth.<br/> <br/>=)</td>', 'People say that brighter colors would have made them like this photo more. To me brighter colors would have made this cliche. It''s the colors that really make this photo. It''s very soothing. Very Silky Smooth. =)', '2007-05-24 02:05:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689530, 509729, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, welcome to DPChallenge.  Congrats on tossing in that first entry.  Now, we look forward to many, many more.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I think that choosing f/11 for this shot was a pretty good idea, thus trying to keep all aspects of the image nicely focused.  Even still, it looks like you were a bit too close to the flower by the fact that you lost focus on the petal in the front.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Your lighting isn''t bad, especially for the harsh, natural lighting that you chose to shoot in.  Still though, the lighting is a touch on the hard side, with bright highlights and hard shadows.  This really takes away from the silky-smooth feel that you were going for.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> While I''m no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I do feel that this is far too centered for such a common-place image.  You''ll find that pictures of flowers and other common subjects will suffer in their score around here unless the image and the composition are both very spectacular.  I do agree with dtremain that this would have been stronger with a square crop.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> 5.15 is a pretty strong place to start with a first entry.  That leaves much room for improvement, but it also shows that the voters didn''t absolutely hate what you offered.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First of all, welcome to DPChallenge.  Congrats on tossing in that first entry.  Now, we look forward to many, many more. Camera Work/Technical: I think that choosing f/11 for this shot was a pretty good idea, thus trying to keep all aspects of the image nicely focused.  Even still, it looks like you were a bit too close to the flower by the fact that you lost focus on the petal in the front. Lighting: Your lighting isn''t bad, especially for the harsh, natural lighting that you chose to shoot in.  Still though, the lighting is a touch on the hard side, with bright highlights and hard shadows.  This really takes away from the silky-smooth feel that you were going for. Composition/Content: While I''m no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I do feel that this is far too centered for such a common-place image.  You''ll find that pictures of flowers and other common subjects will suffer in their score around here unless the image and the composition are both very spectacular.  I do agree with dtremain that this would have been stronger with a square crop. My Opinion: 5.15 is a pretty strong place to start with a first entry.  That leaves much room for improvement, but it also shows that the voters didn''t absolutely hate what you offered. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2007-05-24 02:56:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689557, 512108, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I think that I''ll forgo critiquing this image and offer you some friendly advice.  Value every comment you receive, every one of them.  Firing back at those that take time to comment on your images only serves to dissuade the rest of us from offering our opinions.  I looked through each of the comments offered here, and I really can''t see what pissed you off so much.  Looking at the comments and the photo together, I am even more lost.  You said yourself that you felt rushed while shooting, and it really shows.  You entered an image below your capabilities, and you paid the price.  We all do it.  If you don''t  feel that you can subject yourself to comments, critiques and even criticisms, maybe you shouldn''t submit any more.  Sorry to be blunt, but I try to speak the truth.  Good luck with future entries, and I hope that you continue to offer entries.  <br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  I think that I''ll forgo critiquing this image and offer you some friendly advice.  Value every comment you receive, every one of them.  Firing back at those that take time to comment on your images only serves to dissuade the rest of us from offering our opinions.  I looked through each of the comments offered here, and I really can''t see what pissed you off so much.  Looking at the comments and the photo together, I am even more lost.  You said yourself that you felt rushed while shooting, and it really shows.  You entered an image below your capabilities, and you paid the price.  We all do it.  If you don''t  feel that you can subject yourself to comments, critiques and even criticisms, maybe you shouldn''t submit any more.  Sorry to be blunt, but I try to speak the truth.  Good luck with future entries, and I hope that you continue to offer entries.   Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2007-05-24 03:19:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689581, 510842, 46336, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club. </b> <br/> <br/>Hi Joel,<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC. Congratulations on your third challenge entry and new personal best. <br/> <br/>You have very clearly satisfied the challenge with wonderfully smooth flowing water. I personally think your idea of retaining the corroded stone was effective in off-setting the smoothness of the water, but do agree with comments that imagewould be better if the leaves on the left were excluded. Other than that the composition is not overwhelmignly engaging, I think due to a lack of clear focal point - without the title and challeneg I wouldn''t conclude that you were trying to tell me anything about smoothness. <br/> <br/>This is a technically sound shot. With ISO at 100, your aperture at F/22, and using an ND filter I see that you have already doen loads to try drag out the shutter. <br/> <br/>It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges. <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Paul</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.   Hi Joel, Welcome to DPC. Congratulations on your third challenge entry and new personal best.  You have very clearly satisfied the challenge with wonderfully smooth flowing water. I personally think your idea of retaining the corroded stone was effective in off-setting the smoothness of the water, but do agree with comments that imagewould be better if the leaves on the left were excluded. Other than that the composition is not overwhelmignly engaging, I think due to a lack of clear focal point - without the title and challeneg I wouldn''t conclude that you were trying to tell me anything about smoothness.  This is a technically sound shot. With ISO at 100, your aperture at F/22, and using an ND filter I see that you have already doen loads to try drag out the shutter.  It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges.  CheersPaul', '2007-05-24 03:40:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689712, 512441, 18450, '<td valign="top">I''m sorry about your DQ. This is such a beautiful image...... I''m looking forward to seeing more of your work, and sure we''ll soon see you on the front page of the forum again.</td>', 'I''m sorry about your DQ. This is such a beautiful image...... I''m looking forward to seeing more of your work, and sure we''ll soon see you on the front page of the forum again.', '2007-05-24 05:46:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689745, 512441, 68426, '<td valign="top">Fabulous photograph.</td>', 'Fabulous photograph.', '2007-05-24 06:17:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689855, 512545, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I''ve no doubt that this cat is exceptionally smooth and silky to the touch - all your photographs of her really emphasize the delightful nature of her markings and fur (and personality, I might add!)  You''re right, though in that this probably isn''t the best shot you''ve had of her, but I like the fact she seems to be quite enjoying the spot of sunshine - a very familiar pose for cat owners everywhere.  A very well distributed bell curve on the score  - you met the challenge, but as you say, failed to "wow" voters.<br/> <br/>I never tire of seeing pictures of her, so keep entering them!  (I particularly love the one where she''s leaping into the picture - still one of my favs of yours!)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club I''ve no doubt that this cat is exceptionally smooth and silky to the touch - all your photographs of her really emphasize the delightful nature of her markings and fur (and personality, I might add!)  You''re right, though in that this probably isn''t the best shot you''ve had of her, but I like the fact she seems to be quite enjoying the spot of sunshine - a very familiar pose for cat owners everywhere.  A very well distributed bell curve on the score  - you met the challenge, but as you say, failed to "wow" voters. I never tire of seeing pictures of her, so keep entering them!  (I particularly love the one where she''s leaping into the picture - still one of my favs of yours!)', '2007-05-24 08:03:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689872, 512529, 30982, '<td valign="top">Guten tag from the Critique Club!  <br/> <br/>(And no, I don''t speak much German yet but am trying to learn.)<br/> <br/>Your score is a good one on this and you definitely met the challenge, not just with the silky nature of her clothing, but with the smooth presentation.  The angle adds a nice bit of tension to the shot; the colors are vibrant and dark, highlighting the smoothness of her clothing material; and the lines formed by her arm and leg provide good balance to the composition.  To have scored higher, a tad bit sharper focus for the picky crowd may have helped (though I like the softness).  And you''ll simply not win over the "hate tilted pictures!" crowd, but as I said, the tilt suits this very well.</td>', 'Guten tag from the Critique Club!   (And no, I don''t speak much German yet but am trying to learn.) Your score is a good one on this and you definitely met the challenge, not just with the silky nature of her clothing, but with the smooth presentation.  The angle adds a nice bit of tension to the shot; the colors are vibrant and dark, highlighting the smoothness of her clothing material; and the lines formed by her arm and leg provide good balance to the composition.  To have scored higher, a tad bit sharper focus for the picky crowd may have helped (though I like the softness).  And you''ll simply not win over the "hate tilted pictures!" crowd, but as I said, the tilt suits this very well.', '2007-05-24 08:09:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689899, 510276, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Initial reaction was a good one - very smooth, very silky in overall effect, so I''d say you met the challenge well.  There is a bit of unnecessary tension created by cropping off her elbow on the left side of the picture - I think that one little thing disrupts the flow of the image a bit.  Your commenters liked it very well and you did an excellent job with the light - adding to your notes that you used fabric over the onboard flash is a good learning tip for others.  Good use of shadow, nice rich, warm color.<br/> <br/>Your score is pretty good in my opinion (more 6s than 5s and more 7s than 4s) and may have been a bit higher had you not cropped the elbow.  There are some factions who don''t like photographs of art or sculptures regardless of how well they''re presented - you''ll simply not win them over.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Initial reaction was a good one - very smooth, very silky in overall effect, so I''d say you met the challenge well.  There is a bit of unnecessary tension created by cropping off her elbow on the left side of the picture - I think that one little thing disrupts the flow of the image a bit.  Your commenters liked it very well and you did an excellent job with the light - adding to your notes that you used fabric over the onboard flash is a good learning tip for others.  Good use of shadow, nice rich, warm color. Your score is pretty good in my opinion (more 6s than 5s and more 7s than 4s) and may have been a bit higher had you not cropped the elbow.  There are some factions who don''t like photographs of art or sculptures regardless of how well they''re presented - you''ll simply not win them over.', '2007-05-24 08:22:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3689928, 512197, 12611, '<td valign="top">The log and the expression are killer; it borders on something naughty, but it also technically set up well; something for everyone in other words!<br/></td>', 'The log and the expression are killer; it borders on something naughty, but it also technically set up well; something for everyone in other words!', '2007-05-24 08:41:12.000000', NULL, 0),
